From: Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 01:45:39 +0000
Subject: Request the reboot or shutdown only once

end_phase() is called again each time a client exits during the EXIT
phase, and each call reached csm_manager_quit(). Under Unity, where many
clients go away at once, a restart was requested twelve times in 120 ms
on target; logind refused all but the first with OperationInProgress,
and cinnamon-session took the refusal as a failed restart. With the
PrepareForShutdown backport that meant quitting on a false "not
confirmed by logind" instead of on logind's signal.

Assisted-by: LLM claude-opus-5-5
---
 cinnamon-session/csm-manager.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cinnamon-session/csm-manager.c b/cinnamon-session/csm-manager.c
index 5855734..7620661 100644
--- a/cinnamon-session/csm-manager.c
+++ b/cinnamon-session/csm-manager.c
@@ -158,6 +158,7 @@ struct CsmManagerPrivate
         CsmLogoutAction         dialog_action;
 
         gboolean                dbus_disconnected : 1;
+        gboolean                quit_requested : 1;
         guint                   name_owner_id;
 
         ca_context             *ca;
@@ -485,6 +486,12 @@ csm_manager_quit (CsmManager *manager)
         /* See the comment in request_reboot() for some more details about how
          * this works. */
 
+        /* end_phase() runs again for every client that exits during the
+         * EXIT phase; request the reboot or shutdown once. */
+        if (manager->priv->quit_requested)
+                return;
+        manager->priv->quit_requested = TRUE;
+
         csm_store_clear (manager->priv->inhibitors);
 
         switch (manager->priv->logout_type) {
